The Haber process is usually carried out at a temperature of approximately $400^{\circ}\text{C}$ in the presence of a catalyst. Changing the temperature affects both the rate of production of ammonia and the yield of ammonia.

The Boltzmann distribution for a mixture of nitrogen and hydrogen at $400^{\circ}\text{C}$ is shown. $E_{\text{a}}$ represents the activation energy for the reaction.

